From: royka1 <397414+royka1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 13:52:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 21/46] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8475: Use the PCIe0 controller MSIs

MSIs from the PCIe0 endpoint never arrive through the GIC ITS on SM8475;
ath11k's MHI boot times out waiting for them. The vendor kernel uses
SPI-based MSI too. Drop msi-map so the DWC controller's msi0..7
interrupts are used. Device-tested with a QCA6490.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475.dtsi | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475.dtsi
index 6f47cb2f0..2f5b29ba1 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475.dtsi
@@ -61,6 +61,16 @@ &dispcc {
 	compatible = "qcom,sm8475-dispcc";
 };
 
+/*
+ * MSIs from the endpoint never reach the GIC ITS on SM8475 (the vendor kernel
+ * uses SPI-based MSI as well): ath11k's MHI boot times out. Use the
+ * controller's own MSI interrupts.
+ */
+&pcie0 {
+	/delete-property/ msi-map;
+	/delete-property/ msi-map-mask;
+};
+
 /* SM8475 PCIe0 has a V6 gen3x2 PHY wired as one lane */
 &pcie0_phy {
 	compatible = "qcom,sm8475-qmp-gen3x1-pcie-phy";
